# c1: slot-timing
seg-1f2727dc4ca4 = The <c1/> scenario kind answers three questions for a clock that free-runs between synchronisations and must keep traffic inside a <b>time-indexed slot</b>: a routing, tasking or contact slot whose <b>guard</b> is the largest absolute time error, on either side, at which the slot still works.

# text
seg-6b39d8afeb5d = <b>When does the guard break?</b> Seconds from the last fix until the predicted time error reaches the guard, with every contributing term itemised and the dominant one named.

# text
seg-60476d723e1a = <b>How much time is left now?</b> The same figure minus the time already elapsed since the fix.

# text
seg-84010982db35 = <b>How often must the clock take a fix?</b> The largest interval between fixes that keeps the error inside the guard, net of the latency before a fix takes effect.

